  "reason": "The qualified_original assertion claims that the SOURCE (cytoplasm) contains TARGET (motor proteins) which 'move along microtubules to transport essential proteins'. The qualified_proposal assertion claims that the SOURCE (cytoplasm) contains TARGET (motor proteins) which 'serve as tracks for intracellular transport'. This creates a concrete claim difference: the original explicitly attributes the action of moving and transporting to the motor proteins, whereas the proposal incorrectly attributes the function of serving as tracks to the motor proteins themselves. In biological reality, microtubules serve as tracks, while motor proteins move along them; the proposal's definition misidentifies the role of the target entity (motor proteins) by assigning it the structural function of the track"
